From dbad0d7199ac7d0e3230c0ac8af78df0cdf78518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:28:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 44/46] freebsd: block volumes and formatted local disks

FreeBSD has no block devices; disks are character devices in devfs.

- hostutil: a character device that is a GEOM provider (disk, partition,
  label, md(4), ZFS volume) is a BlockDevice, read from
  kern.geom.conftxt without opening it. Local PVs of a disk, block-mode
  volumes and HostPathType BlockDevice now take FreeBSD disks.
- volumepathhandler: nullfs can't mount a device node, so the per-pod
  references below the global map path are symbolic links to the device,
  counted as such; no loop device is attached as a lock (md(4) can't
  stack on a device); FindGlobalMapPathUUIDFromPod follows the links.
- mount-utils: format and check like Linux (blkid, mkfs.ext4 and e2fsck
  from e2fsprogs; newfs and fsck_ufs for ufs), mount ext2/3/4 as ext2fs.
- e2e: loop devices are md(4) vnode disks (mdconfig), blockfs is ext4
  mounted with ext2fs, and the volume mode check expects a character
  device on FreeBSD nodes.
